                <pb facs="0448" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-12T17:00:00-05:00">April 12, 1940—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. The British Ambassador has informed the Department that instructions have now
                    been issued to the British Minister in Guatemala to undertake conversations or
                    negotiations on the Belize dispute with the Guatemalan Foreign Minister with a
                    view to finding a way out of the present impasse.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
